type: article
title: "Rigidity of Pattern-Avoiding Breadth-First Reading Words of Increasing Trees"
authors:
  - family-names: "Bona"
    given-names: "Victor"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Blumenau, Brazil"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
version: "1.1.0"
url: "https://github.com/vicotrbb/bfs-avoidance-frontier"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vicotrbb/bfs-avoidance-frontier"
keywords:
  - enumerative combinatorics
  - pattern avoidance
  - increasing trees
  - k-ary heaps
  - breadth-first search
  - OEIS
  - Lean 4
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >
  For every branching bound k, 312-avoiding BFS realizability collapses to
  the complete k-ary heap shape, and 231-avoiding words of length 1 modulo
  k admit full k-ary realizations. Parent-sequence proofs yield binary OEIS
  identities, supported by formal proofs and reproducible enumeration.
